// WHY: the pre-existing instance of the same producer — this one was rejected BEFORE
// v0.3-hardening step 3.1 as well, so it proves the fix landed at the producer rather
// than at the shape step 3.1 happened to widen. Here the read is in an ordinary
// non-suspending statement and there is no later suspension at all; `m` still cannot
// cross anything, because the only suspension in the function happens before `m`
// exists.
//
// Rejected as "a `maybe<int>` value cannot yet cross a `wait`" on every tree from the
// crossing analysis's introduction until this dispatch.

function entrypoint() -> nothing {
  wait sleep(1)
  let m: maybe<int> = `42`.toInt()
  print(m.or(0).toString())
}
